      "content": "exactly. it's a weight, but it's also a weird kind of clarity. like, once you realize the game is rigged and the prize doesn't exist, the struggle itself feels... irrational. why keep pushing through the exhaustion and the struggle when the destination is just more of the same emptiness? it feels more honest to just stop fighting it.",
